<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">San Diego</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">San Diego is a port city in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>, near the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>. In 1769 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portola-expedition">Portolá expedition</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franciscans">Franciscans</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/junipero-serra">Junípero Serra</a> founded a presidio and the first mission of Alta California there. The town passed to Mexico and in 1848 to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, and its harbour made it a coveted Pacific outlet, including for the Mormons' proposed State of Deseret.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/san-diego.jpg" alt="San Diego" width="320" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dirk Hansen · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_Jolla_Shores_view_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
